<p class="imageCaption">Footage exhibits the Russian acrobat, named Darina, hooked up to the metallic bar by her hair in Shanghai on January 21</p>
</div>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">The performer, who&#8217;s a part of the Shanghai Circus, mentioned she was practising her act throughout her downtime. </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">She had a name from baffled Shanghai Metro managers asking her what she was doing and why she was hanging by her hair. </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">Darina mentioned: &#8216;I&#8217;ve been practising this transfer for half a 12 months. I wish to remind everybody that it was a harmful trick and shouldn&#8217;t be tried if untrained.&#8217; </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">Individuals had been left baffled by the stunt, worrying that she was going to harm herself or her scalp. </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">She shared the clip on Douyin, the Chinese language model of TikTok, after practising the stunt for greater than half a 12 months.     </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">The performer has shared related clips on her feed lately of her hair hanging and didn&#8217;t anticipate the footage to garner a lot consideration. </p>
<p class="mol-para-with-font">Darina has been a circus performer since 2013 and invited folks to look at her present. </p>
